WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
A vehicle zone today is a relay box and a loom of

2
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:03.680
wires.

3
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:09.860
Replace it with one chip and brake messages and comfort traffic now

4
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.500
share the same silicon.

5
00:00:11.535 --> 00:00:16.475
Ethernet, CAN, LIN and FlexRay all arrive at one gateway,

6
00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:21.975
which rate-limits each domain, so a flood on one bus cannot starve

7
00:00:21.975 --> 00:00:22.635
another.

8
00:00:22.645 --> 00:00:27.245
A switch that keeps precise time reserves slots for brake-by-wire on a

9
00:00:27.245 --> 00:00:31.245
shared link, so its latency is bounded by hardware,

10
00:00:31.245 --> 00:00:33.325
not by software scheduling.

11
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.753
A router turns each incoming message into a request,

12
00:00:36.753 --> 00:00:39.973
and hands it to whichever block will act on it.

13
00:00:40.653 --> 00:00:43.553
Every message rides the same crossbar.

14
00:00:43.553 --> 00:00:48.878
Sixteen smart fuses replace the relay box, switching 12 and 48 volt

15
00:00:48.878 --> 00:00:52.028
loads right beside the logic that commands them.

16
00:00:52.039 --> 00:00:54.319
Two cores run in lockstep.

17
00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:57.459
A mismatch drives the zone to its safe state,

18
00:00:57.459 --> 00:01:01.319
and a firewall keeps lighting away from safety registers.

19
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.580
Every image is checked before it runs, and a failed update rolls

20
00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.820
back, so a bad update never replaces the working bank.

21
00:01:09.831 --> 00:01:11.831
SKU-9 is pre-silicon.

22
00:01:11.831 --> 00:01:16.531
Its highest safety level is a design target here,

23
00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:17.331
not a certificate

24
00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.031
Bring us your zone's loads and networks.

25
00:01:21.031 --> 00:01:24.911
We will tell you what SKU-9 must prove.
